    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_4a449905",
      "@type": "EmotionExpression",
      "instance_name": "mocking_applause",
      "label": "mocking approval expression",
      "description": "The image conveys a tone of ironic or dismissive approval, as suggested by the text overlay 'damn girl' and 'that's a policy i could get behind.' The slight smile on Bill Clinton's face, combined with the casual phrasing, suggests a tone that is not serious or respectful, but rather mocking or flippant. This emotional expression is derived from the juxtaposition of a formal political figure with a colloquial, almost dismissive endorsement, implying a lack of genuine commitment or seriousness toward the policy being referenced.",
